      ":question/id": "546eb8a6-49a5-5143-9a07-6f53ec41e0cc",
      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle\\int \\left(-2+t^{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t=$\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(-2+t^{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(-2+t^{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -2\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t+\\int t^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= -2\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+\\frac{t^{4+1}}{(4+1)}+C \\\\ &= -2t+\\frac{t^{5}}{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
